IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`
IMPORT `sgba-i-s549-2012`
IMPORT `sgba-i-s559-2010`
IMPORT `sgba-versions`

-- Tests for sgba-versions.l4 and the two notification modules. Every expected value is written from the Gazette text:
-- the First Schedule of the Revised Edition 2003 (31 July 2003) and of the Revised Edition 2012 (31 August 2012) lists 1. broadcast television receiver, 2. broadcast sound receiver, 3. TVRO system;
-- S 549/2012 (made 30 October 2012, first published 31 October 2012, "deemed to have come into operation on 1st January 2011") substitutes a First Schedule listing only the TVRO system;
-- the Third Schedule of the Revised Edition 2003 names Starhub Cable Vision Ltd.; S 559/2010 (first published 30 September 2010, in operation 1 October 2010) names StarHub Cable Vision Ltd. and SingNet Pte. Ltd.

§ `Which version is read: the conduct day and the reading day`

GIVEN c IS A DATE
      r IS A DATE
GIVETH A STRING
`the source of the First Schedule version read` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the First Schedule version read for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` c r
    WHEN NOTHING THEN "NOTHING"
    WHEN JUST v THEN v's `source`

GIVEN c IS A DATE
      r IS A DATE
GIVETH A STRING
`the source of the Third Schedule version read` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Third Schedule version read for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` c r
    WHEN NOTHING THEN "NOTHING"
    WHEN JUST v THEN v's `source`

`Revised Edition 2003 text` MEANS "Revised Edition 2003 (31 July 2003), e-Gazette"
`Revised Edition 2012 text` MEANS "Revised Edition 2012 (31 August 2012), e-Gazette"
`S 549 text` MEANS "S 549/2012, made 30 October 2012, first published 31 October 2012 at 5.00 pm, deemed in operation from 1 January 2011"
`consolidation text` MEANS "Informal consolidation in force from 25 September 2024, Singapore Statutes Online rendering"

-- before any text exists: a conduct day or a reading day before 31 July 2003 answers NOTHING
#ASSERT `the source of the First Schedule version read` (Date 30 7 2003) (Date 1 1 2005) EQUALS "NOTHING"
#ASSERT `the source of the First Schedule version read` (Date 1 9 2003) (Date 30 7 2003) EQUALS "NOTHING"
#ASSERT `the source of the First Schedule version read` (Date 1 1 2002) (Date 1 1 2002) EQUALS "NOTHING"
#ASSERT `the source of the First Schedule version read` (Date 31 7 2003) (Date 31 7 2003) EQUALS `Revised Edition 2003 text`
-- the Revised Edition 2003 governs until the Revised Edition 2012 and S 549/2012 are published
#ASSERT `the source of the First Schedule version read` (Date 5 5 2005) (Date 1 6 2005) EQUALS `Revised Edition 2003 text`
#ASSERT `the source of the First Schedule version read` (Date 31 12 2010) (Date 1 1 2012) EQUALS `Revised Edition 2003 text`
#ASSERT `the source of the First Schedule version read` (Date 31 12 2010) (Date 15 11 2012) EQUALS `Revised Edition 2003 text`
-- conduct on 1 January 2011 (the day S 549/2012 is deemed to take effect), read before and after it is published
#ASSERT `the source of the First Schedule version read` (Date 1 1 2011) (Date 1 1 2012) EQUALS `Revised Edition 2003 text`
#ASSERT `the source of the First Schedule version read` (Date 1 1 2011) (Date 15 9 2012) EQUALS `Revised Edition 2003 text`
#ASSERT `the source of the First Schedule version read` (Date 1 1 2011) (Date 30 10 2012) EQUALS `Revised Edition 2003 text`
#ASSERT `the source of the First Schedule version read` (Date 1 1 2011) (Date 31 10 2012) EQUALS `S 549 text`
#ASSERT `the source of the First Schedule version read` (Date 1 1 2011) (Date 1 11 2012) EQUALS `S 549 text`
#ASSERT `the source of the First Schedule version read` (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 8 2012) EQUALS `Revised Edition 2003 text`
#ASSERT `the source of the First Schedule version read` (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 15 9 2012) EQUALS `Revised Edition 2003 text`
#ASSERT `the source of the First Schedule version read` (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 15 11 2012) EQUALS `S 549 text`
-- conduct on the day the Revised Edition 2012 is dated, and the day before
#ASSERT `the source of the First Schedule version read` (Date 30 8 2012) (Date 15 9 2012) EQUALS `Revised Edition 2003 text`
#ASSERT `the source of the First Schedule version read` (Date 31 8 2012) (Date 15 9 2012) EQUALS `Revised Edition 2012 text`
