#ASSERT `the Third Schedule in the Revised Edition 2012`'s `published on` EQUALS (Date 31 8 2012)
#ASSERT `the Third Schedule in the consolidation in force from 25 September 2024`'s `takes effect on` EQUALS (Date 25 9 2024)
#ASSERT `the Third Schedule in the Revised Edition 2003`'s `providers of the subscription nationwide television service` EQUALS LIST "Starhub Cable Vision Ltd."
#ASSERT `the Third Schedule in the Revised Edition 2012`'s `providers of the subscription nationwide television service` EQUALS LIST "StarHub Cable Vision Ltd.", "SingNet Pte. Ltd."
#ASSERT `the Third Schedule in the consolidation in force from 25 September 2024`'s `providers of the subscription nationwide television service` EQUALS LIST "StarHub Cable Vision Ltd.", "SingNet Pte. Ltd."
-- the later of two versions is the one published later, and a lone version is itself
#ASSERT (`the later published of two First Schedule versions` `the First Schedule in the Revised Edition 2003` (JUST `the First Schedule as substituted by S 549/2012`)) EQUALS JUST `the First Schedule as substituted by S 549/2012`
#ASSERT (`the later published of two First Schedule versions` `the First Schedule as substituted by S 549/2012` (JUST `the First Schedule in the Revised Edition 2003`)) EQUALS JUST `the First Schedule as substituted by S 549/2012`
#ASSERT (`the later published of two First Schedule versions` `the First Schedule in the Revised Edition 2003` NOTHING) EQUALS JUST `the First Schedule in the Revised Edition 2003`
#ASSERT (`the later published of two Third Schedule versions` `the Third Schedule as substituted by S 559/2010` (JUST `the Third Schedule in the Revised Edition 2003`)) EQUALS JUST `the Third Schedule as substituted by S 559/2010`
#ASSERT (`the later published of two Third Schedule versions` `the Third Schedule in the Revised Edition 2003` (JUST `the Third Schedule as substituted by S 559/2010`)) EQUALS JUST `the Third Schedule as substituted by S 559/2010`
#ASSERT (`the later published of two Third Schedule versions` `the Third Schedule in the Revised Edition 2003` NOTHING) EQUALS JUST `the Third Schedule in the Revised Edition 2003`
-- s 2(1) under a given version, on each reading (the two readings differ only for equipment that is capable of reception and not listed)
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the equipment is broadcasting apparatus under the First Schedule version, reading A` `the First Schedule as substituted by S 549/2012` `equipment used for visual and aural reception` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the equipment is broadcasting apparatus under the First Schedule version, reading B` `the First Schedule as substituted by S 549/2012` `equipment used for visual and aural reception` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the equipment is broadcasting apparatus under the First Schedule version, reading A` `the First Schedule in the Revised Edition 2003` `equipment used for visual and aural reception` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the equipment is broadcasting apparatus under the First Schedule version, reading B` `the First Schedule in the Revised Edition 2003` `equipment that cannot receive a broadcasting service` EQUALS FALSE

§ `The last day the sources were checked (4 November 2026, assumed, not ruled)`

-- "Today" is answered from the latest version deposited, up to and including the day the sources were last checked; a reading day after it answers NOTHING.
#ASSERT `the source of the First Schedule version read` (Date 1 6 2019) (Date 3 11 2026) EQUALS `S 549 text`
#ASSERT `the source of the First Schedule version read` (Date 25 9 2024) (Date 3 11 2026) EQUALS `consolidation text`
#ASSERT `the source of the First Schedule version read` (Date 25 9 2024) (Date 4 11 2026) EQUALS `consolidation text`
#ASSERT `the source of the First Schedule version read` (Date 1 6 2019) (Date 5 11 2026) EQUALS "NOTHING"
#ASSERT `the source of the First Schedule version read` (Date 3 11 2026) (Date 3 11 2026) EQUALS `consolidation text`
#ASSERT `the source of the Third Schedule version read` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 3 11 2026) EQUALS `consolidation text`
#ASSERT `the source of the Third Schedule version read` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 5 11 2026) EQUALS "NOTHING"
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the equipment is broadcasting apparatus, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day, reading A` (Date 1 6 2019) (Date 3 11 2026) `equipment used for visual and aural reception` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the equipment is broadcasting apparatus, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day, reading A` (Date 1 6 2019) (Date 3 11 2026) `equipment capable of direct reception from a satellite` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the equipment is broadcasting apparatus, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day, reading A` (Date 1 6 2019) (Date 5 11 2026) `equipment capable of direct reception from a satellite` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 20(1)(c): the premises phrase (fork F-BA-03), reading A and reading B`

-- Reading A (the default) reads "on any premises in Singapore owned or occupied by the person" as qualifying both "operate" and "have"; reading B reads it as qualifying only "have", so "operate" is not confined to the person's own premises.
`operating it away from my own premises` MEANS
    `Dealing with apparatus` WITH `installs it in a place, or on board a ship, aircraft or vehicle registered in Singapore` IS FALSE
                                , `imports it, offers it for sale, sells it, or has it in possession with a view to sale` IS FALSE
                                , `operates it` IS TRUE
                                , `has it` IS FALSE
                                , `the place is premises in Singapore owned or occupied by the person` IS FALSE
                                , `broadcasting services are received on or by it` IS TRUE

`having it away from my own premises` MEANS
    `Dealing with apparatus` WITH `installs it in a place, or on board a ship, aircraft or vehicle registered in Singapore` IS FALSE
                                , `imports it, offers it for sale, sells it, or has it in possession with a view to sale` IS FALSE
                                , `operates it` IS FALSE
                                , `has it` IS TRUE
                                , `the place is premises in Singapore owned or occupied by the person` IS FALSE
                                , `broadcasting services are received on or by it` IS TRUE

-- 2005, read in 2005, equipment used for visual and aural reception, no licence and no exemption: both readings of F-BA-01 and both of F-BA-03
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the person contravenes section 20(1)(a), (b) or (c), for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day, reading A` (Date 5 5 2005) (Date 1 6 2005) `equipment used for visual and aural reception` `operating it away from my own premises` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the person contravenes section 20(1)(a), (b) or (c), for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day, reading A, reading B of F-BA-03` (Date 5 5 2005) (Date 1 6 2005) `equipment used for visual and aural reception` `operating it away from my own premises` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the person contravenes section 20(1)(a), (b) or (c), for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day, reading B` (Date 5 5 2005) (Date 1 6 2005) `equipment used for visual and aural reception` `operating it away from my own premises` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the person contravenes section 20(1)(a), (b) or (c), for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day, reading B, reading B of F-BA-03` (Date 5 5 2005) (Date 1 6 2005) `equipment used for visual and aural reception` `operating it away from my own premises` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- having it away from the person's own premises is within neither reading
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the person contravenes section 20(1)(a), (b) or (c), for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day, reading A` (Date 5 5 2005) (Date 1 6 2005) `equipment used for visual and aural reception` `having it away from my own premises` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the person contravenes section 20(1)(a), (b) or (c), for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day, reading A, reading B of F-BA-03` (Date 5 5 2005) (Date 1 6 2005) `equipment used for visual and aural reception` `having it away from my own premises` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a licence, or an exemption, takes the person out on reading B too
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the person contravenes section 20(1)(a), (b) or (c), for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day, reading A, reading B of F-BA-03` (Date 5 5 2005) (Date 1 6 2005) `equipment used for visual and aural reception` `operating it away from my own premises` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the equipment must still be listed in the First Schedule version read (reading A of F-BA-01): the version read for these days lists equipment capable of direct reception from a satellite and does not list equipment used for visual and aural reception
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the person contravenes section 20(1)(a), (b) or (c), for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day, reading A, reading B of F-BA-03` (Date 1 6 2019) (Date 3 11 2026) `equipment used for visual and aural reception` `operating it away from my own premises` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the person contravenes section 20(1)(a), (b) or (c), for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day, reading A, reading B of F-BA-03` (Date 1 6 2019) (Date 3 11 2026) `equipment capable of direct reception from a satellite` `operating it away from my own premises` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the person contravenes section 20(1)(a), (b) or (c), for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day, reading B, reading B of F-BA-03` (Date 1 6 2019) (Date 3 11 2026) `equipment used for visual and aural reception` `operating it away from my own premises` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
